KEYWORDS

abf_mode - ABF mode if \zeta or \zeta(\q)
---------------------
integer, scalar
values:
1  - ABF 1D reaction coordinate depending on atomic cooordinate. 
     e.g. migration of the vacancy
2  - ABF 1D alchemical reaction coordinate. e.g. Frenkel-Ladd or other external reaction coordinate which 
     does not depends on the atomic coordinates.   
22 - ... nD alchemical reaction coordinate (under developpement, not working) 

abf_type - way to integrate ABF
---------------------
integer, scalar
values:

1  - brute force (not working)
2  - ABF BIN
3  - ABF BIN OMEGA
4  - ABF GAUSSIAN (not working)
5  - ABF EE
6  - ABF EE   with constant bias (only when compute_mode=3 and abf_mode=2)
7  - ABF (?BIN) dynamics with constant bias (only when compute_mode=3 and abf_mode=2)
8  - restart ABF_EE simulation. The program will read the meanforce_input file into the mean_force_ABFee vector.
     for the case ABF EE From the beginning we will give the 

compute_mode - type of simulation
----------------------
integer, scalar
values:
1 - one simulation mode. Run over the system nlangevin steps
2 - error analysis. In the future I will delete this option - useless. Can be done easily using scripts
3 - constant bias simulations. Those are working only for the cases abf_type 7 and 8

itype_reaction     
---------------------
integer, scalar
values: 
0 - user defined reaction coordinate as is done in reaction.f90
1 - TJS style ... in developpement

nwrite_histo
----------------------
integer  
The frequency of writing on run histograms / unbiased free energy

